WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Here's the problem.

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:04.287
Ansible has no agent and
no record of its own.

3
00:00:04.287 --> 00:00:07.762
It connects, does what the
playbook says, and leaves.

4
00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:11.800
That makes it wonderfully flexible,
and it makes collisions invisible.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.006
Point it at a server that
Azure machine configuration

6
00:00:15.006 --> 00:00:17.500
already governs, and neither tool notices.

7
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.053
Turn on auto-correct, and the
setting quietly flips back,

8
00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.675
with no report that it did.

9
00:00:22.675 --> 00:00:27.225
Two tools can fight over one value
forever while both report success.

10
00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:29.207
The guide's answer is simple:

11
00:00:29.207 --> 00:00:32.913
one owning tool per setting,
written down in the C M D B.

12
00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:35.260
First, what Ansible actually is.
